ication recovery, and concurrent publication idempotency on the P2R2 atomic lock bootstrap without touching real data or KBase content.","outcome":"PASS","phase":"P2","plan_version":"V3.4.2-P0R2","reason_codes":[],"report_payload_sha256":"22e11ac19a35bf4f17543eeff3a1485f6a8d174e1c1871cd3b1b865ca8dc132b","requirements":{"required_evidence_ids":["p2r2-authorization","implementation-baseline","p2r2-t1-task-report","p2r2-t1-completion","attempt-001-incident","attempt-001-t2-validation-source","attempt-001-t2-review-source"],"required_review_receipt_ids":["independent-p2r2-read-lease-fencing-review"],"required_test_receipt_ids":["immutable-release-read-lease-tests","generation-publish-pending-tests","p2r2-t2-regression-tests"]},"review_findings":[{"finding_id":"P2R2-T2-REVIEW-001","resolution":"Accepted as bounded behavior: GenerationPublisher durably records PUBLISH_PENDING before calling ImmutableReleaseStore.promote, so a generation publication WAL cannot exist without its marker. Direct lower-level store recovery remains the T1 seam.","review_receipt_id":"independent-p2r2-read-lease-fencing-review","severity":"NON_BLOCKING","status":"RESOLVED","summary":"recover_pending_publication returns immediately when no PUBLISH_PENDING marker exists instead of recovering an unrelated lower-level release WAL."},{"finding_id":"P2R2-T2-REVIEW-002","resolution":"Retained intentionally as fail-closed wording: the pending identity is preserved and explicit reconciliation is required; no generation or evidence is silently discarded.","review_receipt_id":"independent-p2r2-read-lease-fencing-review","severity":"NON_BLOCKING","status":"RESOLVED","summary":"A retained pending intent after an unreconciled publication is reported as a conflict rather than a transient recovery message."},{"finding_id":"P2R2-T2-REVIEW-003","resolution":"This is the intentional private layering boundary: trusted generation consumers use GenerationPublisher and GenerationReadLease; ImmutableReleaseStore remains